{"id":"h1-01-s1","title":"Scalability","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: what scaling means, vertical vs horizontal, stateless services, load balancing and the first bottlenecks. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"what-scalability-means","title":"What scalability means","html":"<p><strong>Scalability is how well a system keeps working when the load grows, without a rewrite.</strong> Load can be requests per second, users, data size or writes per second. A system is scalable if adding resources (money, machines) gives roughly proportional extra capacity.</p>\n<p>It is not the same as \"fast\". A shop with one cashier can be fast for 5 customers and collapse at 500. Speed is latency; scalability is what happens to latency as load rises.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 130\" width=\"600\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Load grows, so the request has to be spread over more machines\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M442 34 L498 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M442 34 L498 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M442 96 L498 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M442 96 L498 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Users</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Load balancer</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"386.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App server 1</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"386.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App server 2</text><rect x=\"498\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"543\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Database</text></svg><figcaption>Load grows, so the request has to be spread over more machines</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 10M users, each opens the app 5 times a day: 50M requests/day, divided by 86,400 s is about 580 requests/s on average. Peak is usually 3x the average, so plan for about 1,700 requests/s. One well-tuned app server handles roughly 500 to 2,000 simple requests/s, so you need 2 to 4 servers plus spare for failures.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> WhatsApp served hundreds of millions of users with very few engineers by keeping each Erlang server small and stateless-ish. Instagram started as one Django app on one machine and scaled by adding servers and caches, not by redesigning.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A restaurant that is full on Saturday: you can hire faster chefs, or open a second kitchen. Scalability is how painless it is to open that second kitchen.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying \"we will scale it\" with no number. Always estimate the load first.</li>\n<li>Mixing up latency and scalability.</li>\n<li>Designing for 1B users on day one; that is over-engineering and costs money.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"vertical-vs-horizontal-scaling","title":"Vertical vs horizontal scaling","html":"<p><strong>Vertical scaling (scale up)</strong> means a bigger machine: more CPU, RAM, faster disk. <strong>Horizontal scaling (scale out)</strong> means more machines behind a load balancer.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Vertical</th>\n<th>Horizontal</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Effort</td>\n<td>Almost none, no code change</td>\n<td>Needs stateless code, a load balancer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Limit</td>\n<td>The biggest machine you can buy</td>\n<td>Practically none</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Failure</td>\n<td>One machine = one big failure</td>\n<td>One of many fails, rest continue</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cost curve</td>\n<td>Gets steeply expensive at the top</td>\n<td>Roughly linear with commodity boxes</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 412 130\" width=\"412\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Scale up: same code, bigger box. Scale out: more boxes.\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 65 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 96 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 96 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Small VM</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Bigger VM</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">VM x3</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"352\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Biggest VM</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"74\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"352\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">VM x30</text></svg><figcaption>Scale up: same code, bigger box. Scale out: more boxes.</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Why the decision matters (gravity).</strong> Vertical is the right first move: it is reversible, cheap in engineering time, and a single Postgres on 64 cores serves a surprising amount of traffic. Horizontal scaling of the <em>database</em> is a one-way door (sharding), so you delay it as long as is sensible. Stack Overflow famously ran on a handful of beefy SQL Server machines for years.</p>\n<p><strong>When it breaks.</strong> Vertical stops at the hardware ceiling and leaves a single point of failure. Horizontal fails if the app keeps state in memory (see next section).</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Buying a bigger truck versus buying more trucks. A bigger truck is simple until the biggest truck is not big enough, or breaks down and everything stops.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Claiming horizontal is always better. At low scale vertical is simpler and cheaper.</li>\n<li>Forgetting that scaling the stateless tier does nothing if the database is the bottleneck.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"stateless-servers","title":"Stateless servers","html":"<p><strong>A stateless server keeps nothing about a user between requests.</strong> Any server can answer any request, because everything it needs comes with the request (a token) or sits in a shared store (database, Redis).</p>\n<p>If server 1 keeps your login session in its own memory, a request that lands on server 2 sees a stranger. The fixes, in order of preference:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Signed token (JWT or opaque ID plus shared store):</strong> the request carries or references the state.</li>\n<li><strong>Shared session store:</strong> Redis holds sessions, all servers read it.</li>\n<li><strong>Sticky sessions:</strong> the load balancer always sends a user to the same server. Easy, but it unbalances load and loses sessions when that server dies.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 634.8 130\" width=\"634.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Stateless: any server works because state lives in the shared store\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M442 34 L498 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M442 34 L498 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M442 96 L498 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M442 96 L498 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Load balancer</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"386.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App server A</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"386.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App server B</text><rect x=\"498\" y=\"43\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"560.4\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redis sessions</text></svg><figcaption>Stateless: any server works because state lives in the shared store</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Config example (typical).</strong> Session TTL 30 min sliding, Redis with <code>maxmemory-policy allkeys-lru</code>, 2 replicas. A session is about 1 KB, so 10M concurrent sessions need about 10 GB of RAM.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Netflix and Uber run their API services stateless so instances can be killed and replaced at any time (autoscaling, spot instances, deployments).</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A bank where any teller can help you because your account is in the shared computer, not in the teller's head. If tellers memorised customers, you could only use one window.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Putting uploads on local disk of an app server; the next request lands elsewhere.</li>\n<li>Using sticky sessions and then being surprised by a hot server after a deploy.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"load-balancing-basics","title":"Load balancing basics","html":"<p><strong>A load balancer (LB) spreads incoming requests over a pool of servers and stops sending traffic to dead ones.</strong></p>\n<p>Choices that matter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Layer 4 (TCP)</strong>: fast and simple, only sees IPs and ports. <strong>Layer 7 (HTTP)</strong>: reads URLs and headers, so it can route <code>/api</code> and <code>/images</code> differently, terminate TLS and do canary releases. Costs more CPU.</li>\n<li><strong>Algorithms:</strong> round robin (default, fine for equal requests), least connections (better when requests vary a lot), consistent hashing (same key to the same server, good for caches).</li>\n<li><strong>Health checks:</strong> for example HTTP <code>GET /health</code> every 5 s, mark unhealthy after 3 failures, healthy after 2 successes. Too aggressive and a slow moment drains the whole pool.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 468.40000000000003 130\" width=\"468.40000000000003\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The LB drops a dead server out of rotation\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Load balancer</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"394\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Healthy server</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"74\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"394\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Dead server</text></svg><figcaption>The LB drops a dead server out of rotation</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> AWS ALB (L7) and NLB (L4), NGINX, HAProxy and Envoy. Google's Maglev and Facebook's Katran are software L4 balancers handling millions of packets/s.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> The host at a restaurant door who sends each group to a table with room, and skips tables that are closed.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Forgetting that the LB itself is a single point of failure; real setups run LBs in pairs or behind DNS/anycast.</li>\n<li>Round robin with long-lived connections (WebSockets): connection counts become uneven.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"where-scaling-breaks-next","title":"Where scaling breaks next","html":"<p>Adding app servers moves the bottleneck. The usual order in which things hit the wall:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>App CPU</strong>: fixed by more servers (cheap).</li>\n<li><strong>Database reads</strong>: fixed by indexes, then a cache, then read replicas.</li>\n<li><strong>Database writes and size</strong>: fixed by vertical scaling, then partitioning/sharding (expensive, hard to undo).</li>\n<li><strong>A single hot key or single region</strong>: fixed by splitting the key, replication and multi-region.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 698 68\" width=\"698\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Typical order of bottlenecks\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M394 34 L450 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M394 34 L450 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M540 34 L596 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M540 34 L596 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App CPU</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">DB reads</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">DB writes</text><rect x=\"450\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"495\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Hot keys</text><rect x=\"596\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"641\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Region</text></svg><figcaption>Typical order of bottlenecks</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The skill the interviewer tests is naming the <em>next</em> bottleneck and the cheapest fix for it, with a number to justify it.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Jumping to sharding and microservices before measuring.</li>\n<li>Not saying what you would measure (CPU, p99 latency, DB connections, replication lag).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Scalability = staying healthy as load grows. Estimate load first (requests/s, peak 3x).</li>\n<li>Scale up first (cheap, reversible); scale out when you hit limits or need availability.</li>\n<li>Horizontal scaling needs stateless servers: state goes in tokens or a shared store.</li>\n<li>A load balancer (L4 vs L7, round robin vs least connections, health checks) spreads traffic, and must itself not be a single point of failure.</li>\n<li>Every fix moves the bottleneck: CPU, then DB reads, then DB writes, then hot keys, then regions. Name the next one.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}